{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 36, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Greg woke up to the blinding white of a loading screen, his fingers numb against the cold sheets of what felt like a hospital bed. He blinked, expecting the familiar ache behind his eyes from last night’s wine, but instead saw a UI bar floating above his chest—health, stamina, skills—and beneath it, a message in jagged, capitalized letters: **\"LEVEL 1 – CHARACTER CREATED.\"** He bolted upright, only to realize the room was a pixelated village square, NPCs milling about in stiff, blocky movements. A young woman in a hood, her voice glitching like a broken speaker, handed him a rusted sword. \"The Dark King’s soldiers are coming,\" she whispered. Greg’s stomach dropped as he noticed his own hands—too large, his fingers ending in jagged polygons. He clenched his fists, and the sword in his grip flickered, its edges sharpening from gray to steel.\n\nAs the first shouts of battle echoed through the village, Greg lunged after the hooded woman, his movements jerky, unnatural. He swung the sword too late, missing an enemy’s attack by inches, and took a glancing blow that sent his health bar plummeting. A quick scan of his skills revealed nothing but raw \"Strength\" and a single, grayed-out ability: **\"DODGE (COOLDOWN: 10 SECONDS).\"** Panic set in as he sprinted down a crumbling street, dodging arrows that fizzed against invisible barriers. Then, a glitch—a merchant stall flickered, revealing a back alley where the woman stood waiting, her voice calm. \"You’re new,\" she said, pressing a key into his palm. \"Press it when you need help. But be warned—every time you use it, you lose a memory.\" Greg stared at the key, his reflection warping in its metallic surface, and wondered who he’d have to forget to survive.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Greg", "logprob": -3.965810775756836}, {"token": " woke", "logprob": -1.251341462135315}, {"token": " up", "l